      "role": "user",
      "text": "Guide me again. I don't know what foreshadowing means—explain it simply using the childhood idea, then ask just one useful question."
    },
    {
      "message_id": "033eef87-88c5-44c6-8a03-93d18c465096",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "Foreshadowing means planting a small hint early that matters later. For example, a childhood scene that draws attention to the forbidden drawer could make a later discovery inside it feel prepared rather than sudden. We can try that without deciding what the drawer contains.\n\nIf we keep that childhood idea, what feeling does the forbidden drawer bring up for him?"
    }
  ],
